  "result": "The city\u2019s lost-and-found was underneath the train station, and on Tuesdays it stayed open late for things people weren\u2019t sure they wanted back.\n\nA man came for a trumpet he\u2019d left on the 6:12 twelve years ago.\n\n\u201cDo you still play?\u201d asked the clerk.\n\n\u201cNo,\u201d he said. \u201cThat\u2019s why it took me so long.\u201d\n\nShe brought out the case. He opened it and found, tucked beneath the mouthpiece, a grocery list in his own handwriting: eggs, oranges, call Dad.\n\nHe stood there for a while.\n\n\u201cDid you?\u201d she asked.\n\n\u201cBuy oranges?\u201d\n\nShe let him have that.\n\n\u201cYes,\u201d he said at last. \u201cFrom the platform. He told me to come over Sunday and fix the latch on his shed.\u201d He ran his thumb along the edge of the list. \u201cI\u2019d forgotten we talked that day. I remembered the latch.\u201d\n\nThe clerk fetched a claim form. While he filled it out, she went into the back room and moved a small blue umbrella from the shelf marked *Unclaimed* to the shelf marked *Wednesday*.\n\nThere was no Wednesday shelf. She made a label.",
